WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.682
The Autoroute part gives a content item a URL, and its pattern decides

00:00:05.682 --> 00:00:07.592
what that URL looks like.

00:00:07.592 --> 00:00:12.398
In this video, you write patterns in Liquid, see the URLs they generate,

00:00:12.398 --> 00:00:15.540
define them in code, and load content by URL.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:23.638
A content type with the Autoroute part has a Pattern setting.

00:00:23.638 --> 00:00:27.657
The pattern is a Liquid expression, and the text it renders becomes the

00:00:27.657 --> 00:00:29.171
path of a content item:

00:00:29.171 --> 00:00:31.520
its Permalink, and its URL on the site.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:36.616
The pattern runs when a content item is created or updated, and only

00:00:36.616 --> 00:00:38.377
while its path is empty.

00:00:38.377 --> 00:00:42.371
A path that is already set is kept, so changing a pattern does

00:00:42.371 --> 00:00:44.250
not move existing content.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.121
If another content item already uses the path, the generator appends a dash and a number.

00:00:51.121 --> 00:00:56.275
A permalink can't contain spaces, two slashes in a row, or characters such

00:00:56.275 --> 00:00:59.110
as a question mark, a colon, or a dot.

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:10.108
Inside a pattern, ContentItem is the item being routed, and Model.ContentItem is the same item.

00:01:10.108 --> 00:01:16.905
The display_text filter returns its display text, and slugify lowercases text, replacing spaces

00:01:16.905 --> 00:01:19.530
and most punctuation with dashes.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.361
The container filter returns the list that holds a content item.

00:01:24.361 --> 00:01:28.208
A blog post can build its path from the blog title, a slash,

00:01:28.208 --> 00:01:29.607
and its own title.

00:01:29.607 --> 00:01:32.930
Outside a list, the filter returns the item itself.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.785
A field is read through the Content property, under the part that holds it.

00:01:38.785 --> 00:01:45.150
For a Text field named Color on a Product type, that is ContentItem.Content.Product.Color.Text.

00:01:49.395 --> 00:01:51.777
You set a pattern on the content type.

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:56.810
Under Design, Content Definition, Content Types, open the Product type, and choose Edit

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:58.325
on its Autoroute part.

00:01:58.788 --> 00:02:02.055
The Pattern field holds the Liquid expression.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:08.148
This one slugifies the display text, so a product titled Trail Mug gets the path trail-mug.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.903
Let's add the color on a second line:

00:02:10.903 --> 00:02:14.169
a dash, then the Color field of the product, slugified.

00:02:14.169 --> 00:02:16.740
The line break is removed from the result.

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.416
Liquid is checked when you save.

00:02:19.416 --> 00:02:23.486
A pattern with a syntax error is refused, and the message begins:

00:02:23.486 --> 00:02:26.697
Pattern doesn't contain a valid Liquid expression.

00:02:27.153 --> 00:02:32.429
With the expression repaired, Save stores the setting, and a notification confirms it.

00:02:32.429 --> 00:02:36.443
Content items that get a path afterwards use the edited pattern.

00:02:40.658 --> 00:02:45.085
Let's create a product with the title Trail Mug and the color Forest Green.

00:02:45.085 --> 00:02:49.730
The Permalink field is disabled, because this type doesn't allow a custom path.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.478
Publish saves the product.

00:02:51.936 --> 00:02:55.709
The editor reloads with the Permalink the pattern produced:

00:02:55.709 --> 00:02:57.392
trail-mug-forest-green.

00:02:57.392 --> 00:03:02.616
The slugified title and the slugified color are joined by the dash from the pattern.

00:03:03.083 --> 00:03:07.001
Let's create a second product with the same title and color.

00:03:07.001 --> 00:03:11.156
The path is taken, so the generator appends a dash and a number,

00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:14.243
and the Permalink is trail-mug-forest-green-1.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:18.152
Editing a product does not change a path that is set.

00:03:18.152 --> 00:03:22.341
Let's change the color to Slate Blue and check Refresh the path, a

00:03:22.341 --> 00:03:25.948
checkbox that appears when the type allows path updates.

00:03:25.948 --> 00:03:28.799
After Publish, the path is generated again:

00:03:28.799 --> 00:03:30.370
trail-mug-slate-blue.

00:03:34.589 --> 00:03:39.738
The Blog Post type of the Blog recipe builds its path with the container filter:

00:03:39.738 --> 00:03:43.929
the slugified blog title, a slash, and the slugified post title.

00:03:44.381 --> 00:03:48.090
A post gets its container when you create it from the blog.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:51.400
On the Blog page, Create Blog Post opens the editor.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:55.681
Let's give the post the title Notes from the Orchard, and publish it.

00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:59.825
The Permalink is blog, a slash, and the post title:

00:03:59.825 --> 00:04:02.027
blog/notes-from-the-orchard.

00:04:02.027 --> 00:04:07.078
Created outside the blog, a post has no container, so the filter returns

00:04:07.078 --> 00:04:09.863
the post and its title appears twice.

00:04:14.063 --> 00:04:19.450
In a data migration, AlterTypeDefinitionAsync adds the Autoroute part to a type.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:26.403
WithSettings takes an AutoroutePartSettings object, and its Pattern property holds the Liquid expression.

00:04:27.153 --> 00:04:30.769
A recipe sets the same value in its ContentDefinition step.

00:04:30.769 --> 00:04:34.218
Under the part, AutoroutePartSettings holds the Pattern.

00:04:34.218 --> 00:04:37.333
The Blog recipe defines its Article type this way.

00:04:41.533 --> 00:04:45.635
Content with an Autoroute part can be loaded by its path.

00:04:45.635 --> 00:04:50.519
In Liquid, index the Content object with slug, a colon, and the path.

00:04:50.519 --> 00:04:53.123
Content.Slug takes the path alone.

00:04:53.873 --> 00:05:00.643
In Razor, the Orchard helper has GetContentItemBySlugAsync, which loads the content item for a path.

00:05:00.643 --> 00:05:07.093
Passing true as the second argument loads the most recent version instead of the published one.

00:05:09.093 --> 00:05:13.407
A pattern is a Liquid expression on the Autoroute part of a content type.

00:05:13.407 --> 00:05:16.848
Slugify what it uses, set it in the admin or in code, and

00:05:16.848 --> 00:05:20.343
the path it generates becomes the URL of the content item.

00:05:20.343 --> 00:05:21.763
Thanks for watching.

